{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tailscale/tailscale/pulls/21942","id":5006954032,"node_id":"PR_kwDODihR8s8AAAABKnAOMA","html_url":"https://github.com/tailscale/tailscale/pull/21942","diff_url":"https://github.com/tailscale/tailscale/pull/21942.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/tailscale/tailscale/pull/21942.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tailscale/tailscale/issues/21942","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tailscale/tailscale/pulls/21942/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tailscale/tailscale/pulls/21942/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tailscale/tailscale/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tailscale/tailscale/issues/21942/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tailscale/tailscale/statuses/94498fa7f949ab1471de4f57459dbc95a21d3aec","number":21942,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"ssh/tailssh: route SSH forwarding through the privileged monitor","user":{"login":"raggi","id":348,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/348?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/raggi","html_url":"https://github.com/raggi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raggi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raggi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raggi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raggi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raggi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raggi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raggi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raggi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raggi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Route tailssh's forwarding through the per-connection ssh-monitor, so on unix forwarded sockets are dialed and bound by children with the authenticated local user's credentials, never by root tailscaled.\n\n- unix -L, direct-streamlocal: the lexical allowlist check stays in tailscaled as coarse policy. The allowlist is home, /tmp, and /run/user/<uid>. Relative and abstract paths are rejected. The dial then runs as the user through the monitor. The EvalSymlinks re-validation is dropped, and the kernel's DAC is the boundary. The allowlist is capped. A home directory that cleans to \"/\" or is empty would prefix-match every absolute path, and such an entry is dropped instead. Paths at or beyond the sun_path capacity reject lexically rather than dying at bind or dial with a generic EINVAL.\n- unix -R, streamlocal-forward: the listener is created by a user-cred child with umask-at-bind 0600 and unlink-if-owned. Closing it does not unlink the socket, and the stale file on cancel is accepted.\n- TCP -R, tcpip-forward: a tailssh-owned handler replaces gliderssh's ForwardedTCPHandler. The bind goes through the monitor's listen op with the local user's credentials, so privileged ports fail by kernel construction for non-root-mapped users. Root-mapped users are allowed, as in OpenSSH. Bind addresses are loopback-only unless TS_SSH_FORWARD_GATEWAY_PORTS is set, the equivalent of sshd's GatewayPorts.\n- agent forwarding: the socket and its containing directory are created by a user-cred child, a 0600 socket in a 0700 user-owned directory, instead of a root-run MkdirTemp, Chmod, and Chown sequence. Session-end cleanup is unchanged.\n\nThe monitor is spawned lazily on the first forwarding or agent need, from the tailscaled binary, and closed when the SSH connection ends. closeFwdMonitor latches a closed flag under the fwd lock, so a caller racing the teardown is refused by fwdMonitor, or reads the current state without spawning through fwdMonitorIfAny, instead of respawning a monitor nobody ever closes.\n\nplan9 keeps today's behavior through a build-tagged seam, fwdmonitor.go and fwdplan9.go. There is no monitor on plan9. Unix forwarding is rejected there, and reverse TCP forwarding keeps the gliderssh handler with the mayReversePortForwardTo gate.\n\nTests cover conn-level callbacks against a real monitor and real one-shot fwd children: allowlist rejections, user-owned 0600 sockets, a foreign sticky-dir socket not unlinked, loopback, gateway-ports, and privileged-port TCP binds, agent directory hygiene and cleanup, and TS_SSH_DISABLE_FORWARDING coverage, plus refused respawn after teardown. The unix-fwd root-dial regressions cover a static in-allowlist symlink to a root-owned 0600 canary, which must fail permission denied as the bound user, and a dir-swap race, which must never serve the protected canary.\n\nUpdates tailscale/corp#50380","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-25T17:24:02Z","updated_at":"2026-10-26T03:09:02Z","closed_at":"2026-10-26T03:08:59Z","merged_at":"2026-10-26T03:08:59Z","merge_commit_sha":"eba00ab3638983a0c274e2ea271476c80fcd8acf","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"tailscale:raggi/ssh-20","ref":"raggi/ssh-20","repo":{"id":237523442,"node_id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnkyMzc1MjM0NDI=","name":"tailscale","full_name":"tailscale/tailscale","owner":{"login":"tailscale","id":48932923,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjQ4OTMyOTIz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48932923?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tailscale","html_url":"https://github.com/tailscale","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tailscale/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tailscale/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tailscale/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tailscale/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tailscale/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tailscale/orgs","repos